                              "stroke": {
                                "thickness": 1,
                                "fill": "#E5E2DC"
                              },
                              "padding": [
                                4,
                                8
                              ],
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "id": "BAKjY",
                                  "name": "tag3t",
                                  "fill": "#666666",
                                  "content": "Tutorial",
                                  "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Mono",
                                  "fontSize": 10,
                                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "0JuAE",
                          "name": "content",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "layout": "vertical",
                          "gap": 20,
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "4g6KN",
                              "name": "intro",
                              "fill": "#444444",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "As AI capabilities continue to evolve, the need for sophisticated agent frameworks has never been greater. In this post, I'll walk through building a modular agent system from the ground up, focusing on clean architecture and extensibility.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.7,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "GqYck",
                              "name": "h2_1",
                              "fill": "#1A1A1A",
                              "content": "Why Build Your Own?",
                              "lineHeight": 1.4,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 20,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "Jta23",
                              "name": "para1",
                              "fill": "#444444",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "While there are excellent frameworks like LangChain and AutoGen, building your own helps you understand the core patterns. You'll learn about message passing, tool invocation, context management, and the subtle art of prompt engineering.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.7,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "GnGWV",
                              "name": "h2_2",
                              "fill": "#1A1A1A",
                              "content": "Core Architecture",
                              "lineHeight": 1.4,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 20,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "Zsq4S",
                              "name": "para2",
                              "fill": "#444444",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Our agent consists of three main components: the reasoning loop, the tool registry, and the memory system. Each component is designed to be independently testable and swappable.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.7,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "frame",
                              "id": "vI8JG",
                              "name": "codeBlock",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "fill": "#1A1A1A",
                              "layout": "vertical",
                              "padding": 16,
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "id": "z7lkj",
                                  "name": "codeText",
                                  "fill": "#FDFCF9",
                                  "content": "class Agent:\n  def __init__(self, tools, memory):\n    self.tools = ToolRegistry(tools)\n    self.memory = memory\n    self.llm = LLMClient()\n\n  async def run(self, task: str):\n    context = self.memory.retrieve(task)\n    while not self.is_complete():\n      action = await self.reason(task, context)\n      result = await self.execute(action)\n      context = self.update_context(result)",
                                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                                  "fontFamily": "IBM Plex Mono",
                                  "fontSize": 11,
                                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "rP525",
                              "name": "para3",
                              "fill": "#444444",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "The key insight here is that the agent operates in a continuous loop, reasoning about the current state and deciding what action to take next. This pattern allows for complex, multi-step problem solving.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.7,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "Q0ziI",
                              "name": "h2_3",
                              "fill": "#1A1A1A",
                              "content": "Implementing Tool Calling",
                              "lineHeight": 1.4,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 20,
                              "fontWeight": "600"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "OdFIv",
                              "name": "para4",
                              "fill": "#444444",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Tools are the interface between your agent and the outside world. A well-designed tool registry makes it easy to add new capabilities without modifying the core agent logic.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.7,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "iGp9V",
                              "name": "conclusion",
                              "fill": "#444444",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Building your own agent framework is both educational and practical. While production systems might benefit from battle-tested libraries, understanding these patterns deeply will make you a better AI engineer.",
                              "lineHeight": 1.7,
                              "fontFamily": "Inter",
                              "fontSize": 15,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
